      "writtenOn": "2020-02-14T03:46:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no way for platform VPN profiles to opt out of always on then. Is this expected ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 440,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 440,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "c80c7695ce9dfbab093366e712f8ca110d0ed996",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "71f906cf_1761bd2e",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java",
        "patchSetId": 44
      },
      "lineNbr": 440,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-14T07:47:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes; during design discussions, I think we didn\u0027t quite see any use case for an \"opportunistic\" VPN profile, which seems like it might be the only use case where we would need to be able to opt-out (eg wifi assistant, which probably is the literal only user of that opt-out).\n\nEspecially with the change that apps can remove the profile even if it\u0027s in always-on mode, if an app is very much determined to do so, they could have a foreground service that removes the profile once the conditions are no longer met.\n\nThoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "7b1579f5_7d19c905",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 440,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 440,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "c80c7695ce9dfbab093366e712f8ca110d0ed996",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "058ae5f3_d74038ea",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java",
        "patchSetId": 44
      },
      "lineNbr": 462,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-14T03:46:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change represents an important semantic change for this function : before it could only change its return value for a given package on install boundaries, but now it depends whether the app has registered a profile.\n\nThis is the right thing to do for profiles (in fact, I don\u0027t see how it could work otherwise), but make sure that nobody calling this function depends on this not changing arbitrarily. This is crucial for its call site in ConnectivityService.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 462,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 462,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "c80c7695ce9dfbab093366e712f8ca110d0ed996",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b75c2c9b_259638e4",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java",
        "patchSetId": 44
      },
      "lineNbr": 462,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-14T07:47:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yep. the only caller down to this is Settings, which queries it at VPN page load. Also, based on conversations with the Fi VPN folks, the component providing the VpnService can be enabled/disabled at runtime, and therefore this can change at runtime (not just package install/uninstall)",
      "parentUuid": "058ae5f3_d74038ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 462,
        "startChar": 16,
