    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a3308648_79afadba",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java",
        "patchSetId": 44
      },
      "lineNbr": 573,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-14T03:46:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This implies it\u0027s not possible to have both a profile and a service in the same app, and the profile will be preferred always, at least when it comes to having always on. In other words, I can\u0027t have an app that supports both or the service will stop working.\n\nIs this an existing limitation ? Or if an app has two VPN services do they show both in Settings ? If they do and a fortiori if Settings will show both the profile and the service separately, then this is probably an unacceptable limitation ; if it\u0027s already true that you can\u0027t have two services, then it\u0027s okay-ish but it needs public documentation somewhere.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 573,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 573,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "c80c7695ce9dfbab093366e712f8ca110d0ed996",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c2ac64b_3c781e38",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java",
        "patchSetId": 44
      },
      "lineNbr": 573,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-14T07:47:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, this is both intentional, and an existing limitation; if an app has two VpnService(s), it will only show a single one in Settings, and the one that gets started is (i think?) based on the IntentFilter priorities.\n\nFor the Platform VPN case, we had to choose one, and this seemed the less scary of the two to choose. If the user DOES explicitly want the VpnService version, the app probably should have a toggle, and remove the VpnProfile (\"Snoop on me locally mode\")\n\nI think the Fi VPN currently has two VPNs in the same package, and they have to swap which is enabled in order to change the \"isAlwaysOnPackageSupported\" on the fly.",
      "parentUuid": "a3308648_79afadba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 573,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 573,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "c80c7695ce9dfbab093366e712f8ca110d0ed996",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cb30cbf6_36edea86",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java",
        "patchSetId": 44
      },
      "lineNbr": 693,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-14T03:46:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this needs comments because it looks like this can actually fail to start. Here is why I think it\u0027s fine, please check :\n\n• Callers (especially CS) disable always-on when this returns false.\n• We return false for VpnService iff the service fails to start as in the service is not installed.\n• Platform VPN can\u0027t actually fail in the same way as above.\n• Platform VPN can fail to start for temporary reasons, and they should not disable the always-on bit.\n• There are no permanent reasons Platform VPN can fail (stuff like DNS failure may seem permanent but they are in fact temporary as the name could resolve on some other network)\n• We don\u0027t return false if a Service VPN fails to connect here, only if the package is not installed (how the got here in this case is a mystery though).\n\nPlease check that all the above is true. If it is, add a comment explaining it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 693,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 693,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "c80c7695ce9dfbab093366e712f8ca110d0ed996",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "867dc18e_b8b52c94",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java",
        "patchSetId": 44
      },
      "lineNbr": 693,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-14T07:47:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. This is all true as of the updated patchset, with comments.\n\nThere was one case where the Platform VPN could fail to start if an invalid profile was given (which should be impossible here, given that it was provisioned from an Ikev2VpnProfile in provisionVpnProfile()), which is now checked in the try-catch-finally block.",
      "parentUuid": "cb30cbf6_36edea86",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 693,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 693,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "c80c7695ce9dfbab093366e712f8ca110d0ed996",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e66fd7e3_a05b1537",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java",
        "patchSetId": 44
      },
      "lineNbr": 2881,
